            "messageBody": "After boot the two round panels disagreed: the greeting is drawn on both, then\nonly the state panel was repainted, so one said \"idle\" while the other still\nsaid \"hello vela\".  That reads as a broken panel and was reported as one.\n\nEntering idle now clears the summary panel.  This is not only about boot -- a\nsummary left over from a finished session must not sit next to an idle state,\nor the screen claims something the device is no longer doing.\n\nAn empty line is drawn as just the cleared background, so the same call serves\nas \"blank this panel\".",
