            "messageBody": "Touches only the mailbox transport, whose code belongs to zhaoyutao1, so the\nowner can review it apart from the store that uses it.  It comes first because\nthe flash client added next will not compile without the channel, ACK-state and\nIPC-flag definitions this commit adds to bk7258_mbox.h.\n\nThree defects made the first FLASH_CMD_READ unanswerable, and the failure did\nnot look like a failed read: the transport quarantined the link, the heartbeat\nlapsed, and the CP's 8-second watchdog reset the chip, so the symptom was a\nreboot loop.\n\n  - the ACK header was left in a state the CP rejects;\n  - the response protocol was single-phase where the vendor's mb_ipc expects\n    two phases;\n  - the part_id/addr bit fields were packed wrong, putting the address in the\n    low bits.\n\nA plain transaction timeout no longer tears down the whole link either; only a\nprobe timeout does, because a slow read is not evidence that the transport is\nbroken.",
